 "dur": 64.0,
 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Mayor Doug's flat road turned into a lake. A duck moved in.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.061
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Smooth as a pancake!\" said Doug. So why are real roads higher in the middle?",
   "s": 3.261,
   "e": 6.821
  },
  {
   "text": "Doug cut the ribbon with golden scissors. Four hundred people clapped.",
   "s": 7.121,
   "e": 10.45
  },
  {
   "text": "Next door, Hilda of Humpton built her road with a hump down the middle.",
   "s": 10.65,
   "e": 13.866
  },
  {
   "text": "Doug laughed. \"Her road has a spine!\"",
   "s": 14.066,
   "e": 15.654
  },
  {
   "text": "Hilda didn't argue. She bought a bike.",
   "s": 15.774,
   "e": 17.518
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it rained for a week.",
   "s": 17.718,
   "e": 18.729
  },
  {
   "text": "Day one, puddles. Day three, ankle-deep. Day five, the bus needed a captain.",
   "s": 18.929,
   "e": 22.866
  },
  {
   "text": "The pizza guy delivered by canoe. The fire truck got a paddle.",
   "s": 23.066,
   "e": 26.162
  },
  {
   "text": "Admiral Puddles the duck had always wanted a lake. Now he had one, with traffic.",
   "s": 26.362,
   "e": 30.515
  },
  {
   "text": "So Doug bought a sponge the size of a sofa. \"Smooth as a pancake!\"",
   "s": 30.715,
   "e": 34.347
  },
  {
   "text": "The sponge drank half the road and swelled up like a whale. Then it floated away, with Doug on it.",
   "s": 34.467,
   "e": 38.531
  },
  {
   "text": "Meanwhile in Humpton, Hilda rode her bike to work. Dry socks.",
   "s": 38.731,
   "e": 42.171
  },
  {
   "text": "So what does the hump do?",
   "s": 42.371,
   "e": 43.368
  },
  {
   "text": "Rain hits the high middle and rolls downhill to both edges, into the gutters.",
   "s": 43.668,
   "e": 47.597
  },
  {
   "text": "A flat road has no downhill. The water sits there and soaks in.",
   "s": 47.997,
   "e": 51.324
  },
  {
   "text": "When the lake drained, Flatbury Road looked like Swiss cheese: two hundred potholes. One had a fish in it.",
   "s": 51.524,
   "e": 56.758
  },
  {
   "text": "Doug rebuilt his road with a hump. Admiral Puddles lost his lake.",
   "s": 56.958,
   "e": 60.362
  },
  {
   "text": "So he moved into Doug's bathtub.",
   "s": 60.562,
   "e": 62.015
  }
 ],
